{
  "name": "PaymentsRateTable",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "cohort_key": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Row identity. Online rows: '<provider_slug>|<tier>|<region>' (e.g. 'stripe|ANY|EU'). In-store rows append the channel segment: '<provider_slug>|<tier>|<region>|in_store' (e.g. 'sumup|ANY|EU|in_store'). Provider is 'stripe','paypal','shopify_payments','sumup','stripe_terminal','smile_and_pay','zettle','ANY' (regional fallback). Tier is currently always 'ANY' (Chunk 1b decision \u2014 tier segmentation happens in the engine's savings band, not in the row). Region is 'EU','UK','US','RoW'. Unique per row. Engine lookup: exact match first (e.g. 'stripe|ANY|EU'), then fallback to 'ANY|ANY|<region>' (or 'ANY|ANY|<region>|in_store') if no exact match. M5 (2026-07-24): COUNTRY-pinned rows use the convention '<slug>|<tier>|<REGION>-<CC>' (e.g. 'sumup|ANY|EU-ES') as a HUMAN-READABLE identifier only \u2014 the engine's resolution NEVER parses cohort_key for country; it reads the declared `country` field. Existing keys need no migration."
    },
    "provider_slug": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Stable slug matching the analyzer's provider detection (stripe, paypal, shopify_payments, sumup, stripe_terminal, smile_and_pay, zettle, adyen, mollie, ...). Set to 'ANY' for regional fallback rows."
    },
    "channel": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "online",
        "in_store"
      ],
      "default": "online",
      "description": "Payment channel this row applies to. 'online' = card-not-present (default; every historical/online row leaves this absent and is treated as online). 'in_store' = card-present TPV rows (M4-TPV Fase 2A) \u2014 these carry terminal_rental_monthly_minor + achievable_terminal_rental_monthly_minor and set intl_uplift_bps to null (card-present cross-border volume is negligible for the ICP). The channel is ALSO encoded in cohort_key ('|in_store' suffix) for the engine's exact-match lookup; this declared field makes it queryable/auditable. Purely additive \u2014 no migration."
    },
    "country": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "M5 (2026-07-24) \u2014 OPTIONAL country pin, ISO-3166-1 alpha-2 UPPERCASE ('FR', 'ES'). Absent/null = row valid for the whole region (EVERY pre-M5 row \u2014 no migration). Semantics in the engine's selectRow (payments-gap SYNC block): (1) when the merchant's input carries a country and an active row matches (provider_slug, tier ANY, region, channel) AND row.country === input country, that row WINS over the pan-regional row; (2) a row pinned to a DIFFERENT country is NEVER selected (an ES row must not answer for an FR merchant); (3) the regional fallback chain (ANY|ANY|<region>[|in_store]) stays country-agnostic \u2014 fallback rows must NEVER carry a country. Resolution is FIELD-based: cohort_key is never parsed; the 'REGION-CC' key convention is a readable identifier only. Rationale: verified per-country price divergences inside EU (SumUp 1.75% FR vs 1.49% ES; Zettle FR flat vs ES tiered; Square 1.65% FR vs 1.25% ES) plus single-country providers (MONEI, PAYCOMET, Spanish bank TPV). Seeding of ES rows is a separate chunk (SEED-ES)."
    },
    "tier": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "ANY",
        "PLUS",
        "micro",
        "small",
        "mid",
        "large"
      ],
      "default": "ANY",
      "description": "Revenue tier. Chunk 1b: always 'ANY' \u2014 Stripe/PayPal/Shopify don't publish tiered pricing publicly. Future rows may segment when a provider does (e.g. Shopify tiering by plan). SEED-ES-2 (2026-07-24): 'PLUS' added for PLAN-tier anchor rows (SumUp Pagos Plus ES). A non-ANY tier deliberately keeps the row OUT of selectRow's current-rate resolution (both the M5 countryRow field-match, which requires tier ANY, and the key candidates, which only build '|ANY|' keys) while the multi-anchor pool \u2014 which has no tier filter \u2014 still picks it up as an achievable anchor. This is the sanctioned way to seed subscription-plan anchors without engine changes."
    },
    "region": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "EU",
        "UK",
        "US",
        "RoW"
      ],
      "description": "Geographic region the row applies to."
    },
    "percent_bps": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "Percent component of the effective rate, in basis points. E.g. Stripe EU standard = 150 (1.5%). This is the ATOMIC published percentage \u2014 NEVER blend the fixed fee into this number. The engine amortizes the fixed fee separately using the merchant's real avg ticket at runtime."
    },
    "fixed_fee_minor_units": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "Fixed component of the effective rate, in MINOR units of fixed_fee_currency (cents / pence). E.g. Stripe EU = 25 (i.e. 0.25 EUR). The engine amortizes this against the user's avg_ticket at runtime \u2014 merchants with low tickets pay a much higher effective rate. NEVER pre-amortize into percent_bps."
    },
    "fixed_fee_currency": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "EUR",
        "GBP",
        "USD"
      ],
      "description": "Currency of fixed_fee_minor_units. Determines which minor-unit is used (100 cents = 1 EUR/GBP/USD)."
    },
    "terminal_rental_monthly_minor": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "IN-STORE ONLY (channel='in_store'). Monthly TPV terminal rental in MINOR units of fixed_fee_currency (e.g. 2500 = \u20ac25/mo). 0 for modern TPV providers that sell hardware one-off with no rental (SumUp, Zettle, Smile & Pay, Stripe Terminal). Populated on fallback bank-acquirer rows (BNP, CA, SG, ...) where \u20ac15-40/mo rental is the norm. The engine amortizes this against monthly in-store GMV / ticket at runtime. Absent/null on online rows \u2014 treated as 0. SEED-ES-2 (2026-07-24): ALSO used to model monthly SUBSCRIPTION plans (SumUp Pagos Plus 19\u20ac/mes \u2192 1900) \u2014 economically identical to a rental (fixed monthly cost amortized against GMV), so the engine needs no new field. Purely additive \u2014 no migration."
    },
    "achievable_percent_bps": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "OPTIONAL \u2014 Achievable percent component in bps for the same provider/region after negotiation, in a documented bottom-up breakdown (interchange_cap + scheme_fees + assumed_processor_margin). Null on rows where we have no defensible breakdown. Engine uses this + achievable_fixed_fee_minor_units + same runtime amortization to compute achievable effective rate."
    },
    "achievable_fixed_fee_minor_units": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "OPTIONAL \u2014 Achievable fixed component (usually same or slightly lower than the published fixed fee \u2014 hard to negotiate below scheme minimums). Null when achievable_percent_bps is null."
    },
    "achievable_terminal_rental_monthly_minor": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "IN-STORE ONLY (channel='in_store'). Achievable monthly TPV terminal rental in MINOR units of fixed_fee_currency after migrating to a publicly-contractable modern TPV. Typically 0 (modern TPV = no rental). The recovery narrative for bank-TPV merchants is: migrate to a modern rate AND drop the rental drag \u2014 this field captures the 'after' rental so the engine can amortize the rental delta. Absent/null on online rows \u2014 treated as 0. Purely additive \u2014 no migration."
    },
    "intl_uplift_bps": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "OPTIONAL \u2014 Cross-border card uplift (in bps) charged by this PSP for cards issued outside the merchant's region. Applied to the intl portion of GMV only (percent component; the fixed fee is NOT scaled \u2014 schemes don't charge a separate fixed fee per card origin). Cited verbatim from the PSP's public pricing page via intl_uplift_source_url + intl_uplift_source_quote when known. NULL when the provider does not publish a distinct cross-border rate we could verify \u2014 the engine treats null as 'not modeled' and emits an assumption to that effect (never invents a value in code). ALWAYS null on in-store rows (card-present cross-border is negligible for the ICP). Enmienda 1: NEVER hardcode uplift constants in the engine."
    },
    "achievable_intl_uplift_bps": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "OPTIONAL \u2014 Achievable cross-border uplift (in bps) after negotiation. There is NO public benchmark for negotiated cross-border rates, so this is ALWAYS an assumption \u2014 the row must document the derivation in intl_uplift_assumption_notes (typically: scheme cross-border interchange floor is not negotiable, only the processor's cross-border margin is; achievable \u2248 40-55% of intl_uplift_bps). Null when intl_uplift_bps is null. Engine uses this + intl_uplift_bps to widen the gap on the intl portion of GMV."
    },
    "intl_uplift_source_url": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "OPTIONAL \u2014 Public pricing URL where intl_uplift_bps was cited verbatim. Required when intl_uplift_bps is set and the row is verified=true. Null for rows where the intl uplift is an assumption (fallback rows, or providers without a published cross-border rate)."
    },
    "intl_uplift_source_quote": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "OPTIONAL \u2014 Verbatim quote from intl_uplift_source_url showing the cross-border rate. Required when intl_uplift_source_url is set. Provides audit trail \u2014 if the PSP changes cross-border pricing, we grep this field to find stale rows."
    },
    "intl_uplift_assumption_notes": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "OPTIONAL \u2014 Free-form justification of the intl uplift assumption. REQUIRED when intl_uplift_bps or achievable_intl_uplift_bps carries a derived (not source-quoted) value. Explains the reasoning so the number is auditable in-row, not in code. Enmienda 1: no in-code justification, every assumption lives on the row."
    },
    "verified": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "description": "true = numbers cited verbatim from a public pricing page URL, verified by a human on verified_at. false = regional-average estimate. Engine widens the savings band and injects a mandatory assumption 'Estimate based on regional averages, not provider-verified rates. Connect your PSP for exact figures.' when verified is false."
    },
    "source_url": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The exact URL where percent_bps and fixed_fee_minor_units were read. Required when verified=true. For fallback rows, points to the reference used to derive the average."
    },
    "source_quote": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Verbatim quote from source_url showing the numbers. Required when verified=true. Provides audit trail \u2014 if Stripe changes pricing, we grep this field to find stale rows."
    },
    "source_notes": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Free-form notes: caveats, related premium rates not seeded, TODOs, tier context (e.g. 'Shopify Basic plan rate; Grow/Advanced/Plus tiers not seeded until form asks Shopify plan')."
    },
    "achievable_breakdown_json": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Documented components of achievable_percent_bps. Online shape: { interchange_bps, scheme_fees_bps, processor_margin_bps, processor_margin_band_bps, sources: [{ label, url }] }. In-store shape: { anchor_provider, anchor_region, anchor_percent_bps, anchor_fixed_fee_minor_units, anchor_source_url, anchor_source_quote } \u2014 the publicly-contractable TPV the achievable rate is anchored to. Read by the engine to expose transparency in the output assumptions."
    },
    "savings_band_pct": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "Half-width of the savings uncertainty band, as a fraction. 0.20 = \u00b120% (narrow, verified rows), 0.35 = \u00b135% (wide, fallback rows). Engine uses this to compute lo/hi around the point estimate."
    },
    "verified_at": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "When the human validator confirmed source_quote against source_url. Set by seeder on creation. Rows older than 90 days should be re-validated (future job \u2014 not implemented in Chunk 1b)."
    },
    "active": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": true,
      "description": "Soft-delete flag. Engine only reads active=true rows."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "cohort_key",
    "provider_slug",
    "tier",
    "region",
    "percent_bps",
    "fixed_fee_minor_units",
    "fixed_fee_currency",
    "verified",
    "savings_band_pct"
  ],
  "rls": {
    "read": {},
    "write": {
      "user_condition": {
        "role": "admin"
      }
    }
  }
}